# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites
# checked-out files to CRLF. That is harmless for source Git never executes,
# but a bash script with CRLF endings fails at run time with `$'\r': command
# not found` — an error that points at the shell rather than at the line
# endings, so it reads as a broken script rather than a checkout artefact.
*.sh text eol=lf
